    "kappa/mu/jump_prob are held at the G0 plug-in values; only h is estimated here. A fully observable-only pipeline still needs observable estimators for the latent S dynamics and jump process.",
    "The per-path sigma entering the main-spec likelihood is the simulator oracle (synthetic_env's m.sigma), not an observable; 'observable-only' refers to h, not to sigma. --sigma-mode open estimates sigma from each path's OPEN observations and is a sensitivity; its optimum is flat to optimizer tolerance (~2e-5 in ext_phi across start configurations), so report four decimals only.",
    "jump_prob is the G0 plug-in estimate (0.003) while the simulator truth is 0.005; trimming interacts with this jump-rate misspecification, so the trimmed ext_phi estimate is not a clean function of the true jump process alone.",
